      "body": "2.2.1 features bug fixes and syntax improvements over 2.2.0 (#66).\r\n\r\n**Improvements**\r\n\r\n* Arguments can now be referred to by name in functional math, such as `jacobian`, `functional_gradient` or `hessian`.\r\n* Keyword arguments are now treated the same as positional arguments in functional math and no longer trigger re-tracing of jit-compiled functions.\r\n* Φ-Flow tensors now better integrate with NumPy arrays.\r\n\r\n**Breaking Changes**\r\n\r\n* The gradient function in custom gradient functions must now use dicts.",
